{"agent_id":"pp3g-5WqO-review-r3-big-pickle-live-system-verification-154-3d21","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T04:52:28.286645408Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7f5429e1-0c5e-4e4f-948c-c299661d0bdb","comment_uuid":"7e19b897-a71c-49d1-aa9e-8865f461d002","author":"pp3g-5WqO-review-r3-big-pickle-live-system-verification-154-3d21","content":"## Review Summary: PASS — live-system verification of the compiled fork binary (sha 6e0e282b, 1.18.13-pp3g-fork)\n\nINDEPENDENT live verification against the hang-test harness at /tmp/opencode/matrix-run + /tmp/opencode/live-check (my own probe scripts + full matrix re-run). Binary identity re-verified: sha256 6e0e282bd2ab8ee7913d5cdd552b691c6d3c7e7cde671131ac7dc96fe0103502, --version=1.18.13-pp3g-fork, markers in binary: 'Body read timed out' x2, 'Turn stalled' x1, fork marker x2.\n\n### Focus 1 — non-SSE hang gate: PASS (7/7 runs)\n- 6 targeted row1-equivalent runs + 1 full-matrix row1, ALL: exit=1 (never 124), visible 'Body read timed out' + level=ERROR (message=process error=\"Body read timed out\", stack at compiled bundle chunk-0gzb6ffh.js:439), per-attempt WARN retry attempt=1/2 (nextDelay=2000/4000 honored), terminal 'retry budget exhausted' attempt=3 totalPOSTs=3, wire POSTs=3. Cadence exact: 6s idle + 2s backoff + 6s + 4s + 6s = ~31s.\n\n### Focus 2 — turn-level guard + headerTimeout: PASS\n- row9b PARSE_STALL (SSE :ping keepalives every 500ms, NO data events, experimental.llmIdleTimeout=5000): 'Turn stalled: no parsed stream event within 5000ms' ERROR, exit=1, 3 POSTs. Guard fires ABOVE the raw-body layer — the production 10.9h signature (#39968) — stack shows Stream.timeoutOrElse orElse callback.\n- row3 HANG_MODE=0 (no headers): ProviderHeaderTimeoutError 'response headers timed out after 2000ms' per attempt, exit=1, 3 POSTs, budget exhausted. headerTimeout behavior unchanged.\n\n### Focus 3 — #235 matrix consistency: CONFIRMED (my run: 67/67 vs #235 65/67)\n- Full 16-row matrix re-run on the same binary: 67 checks passed, 0 failed. All rows' pass/fail identical to #235 except the two row1 failures, which did NOT reproduce (my row1 in-matrix: 3 POSTs, invariant held). row8 sensitivity 18<24 (mine) vs 17<23 (#235) — knob tracking consistent.\n\n### Focus 4 — edge probes: PASS\n- healthy JSON/SSE (rows 4/5): exit 0, 1 POST, content delivered via SDK event parts (loop step=1 + exiting loop).\n- slow-but-legit non-SSE (row6): 5s gaps > chunkTimeout=3000 < bodyIdleTimeout=6000 → completes exit 0, NO false-abort, 1 POST (hy3 F2 preserved — the A' idle-progress discriminator works).\n- never-completes slow body (row6b): 2s gaps < idle → 60s total request timeout fires → visible 'The operation timed out.' ERROR, exit=1, 1 POST (bounded+visible).\n- gzip healthy (row10a): exit 0, no ZlibError, content delivered. gzip hang (row10b): 'Body read timed out', exit=1, 3 POSTs.\n- PER_REQUEST isolation (row7): req1 abort does not poison req2; exit 0, 2 POSTs (hy3 F4).\n- OPT-IN confirmed (noIdle probe): without bodyIdleTimeout the SAME hang server's POST hangs the full 60s request timeout (no 6s idle abort) → 'The operation timed out.' → exit 1. Wrapper is genuinely opt-in; even the unconfigured path is now bounded+visible.\n\n### The #235 4-POST-vs-totalPOSTs=3 discrepancy — CLASSIFICATION (my remit)\nThe fork's own retry budget is AIRTIGHT in every observation: attempt=1/2/3 WARNs, nextDelay 2000/4000 honored by fork-sent POSTs, terminal totalPOSTs=3, and fork POST count=3. In #235's single anomaly, the extra wire POST (POST#3) landed 0.94s after the attempt=2 WARN — the fork's declared nextDelay was 4000ms — and the fork's own 3rd POST then landed at the expected time (wire POST#4 at 16:33:15.461, expected 15.426). Therefore the 4th POST is NOT produced by the fork's retry schedule (timing proof), and NOT harness contamination (server log clean, single client run id 4e0a18a8). Most consistent mechanism: a SECOND retry layer (AI-SDK maxRetries) intermittently retrying the ResponseStreamError — matching #235's candidate signature. Frequency: 1 occurrence in 10 row1-equivalent executions across sessions (#226 gate 3, #232 gate 3, #235 matrix 4, my 7 x 3) ≈ 10%. Impact: even in the anomaly case the run terminates bounded+visible (4 wire POSTs then ERROR, exit 1) — the #154 core goal holds unconditionally. The strict wire-level <=3-POST invariant is ~90% reliable on this binary; the fork's own budget (the design deliverable) never breaches.\n\n### NOTABLE POSITIVES\n- Root-cause fix verified at the BINARY level, not just source: the safeIterable consumption-deadlock fix (#232) demonstrably delivers the wrapper error to the consumer (exit 1 + ERROR + budget) — the binary-vs-source divergence saga is resolved.\n- Error visibility is fully realized: per-attempt WARNs + terminal budget WARN + process ERROR on every hang row (7/7 rows in matrix).\n- Numeric chain holds live: detection latency 6s/attempt x 3 POSTs = 18-24s << operator timeouts; never aborts slow-but-progressing bodies.\n- The unconfigured path being bounded+visible (request timeout) is a bonus robustness property I verified live.\n\n### WHAT-NOT-TESTED (negative space, per AGENTS.md)\n- TRUE non-chat requests (e.g., embeddings endpoints) could not be staged through 'opencode run' (chat-only invocation); the dispatcher is content-type-driven (proven live by application/json routing to wrapBodyIdle) and healthy non-SSE controls exercise the same code path, so risk is low — but an embedding-style call is unverified.\n- The 4-POST mechanism attribution to the AI-SDK retry layer is inference from timing evidence, not SDK-internal logs (out of scope); recommended for r2 (#237, AI-SDK second-layer remit) to adjudicate with source.\n- No live install was performed (per brief); PATH opencode remains stock 1.18.13 (verified --version), fork still at /tmp/opencode/fork-build only.\n\n### VERDICT: PASS — the compiled binary behaves as specified across every acceptance criterion: non-SSE hang aborts with visible 'Body read timed out' + level=ERROR + exit 1 (not 124); turn-level guard + headerTimeout fire; matrix consistent (67/67 on my run); edge probes (gzip, slow-legit, healthy controls, opt-in, per-request isolation) all pass. ONE non-blocking finding: the wire-level <=3-POST invariant has a ~10% intermittent overshoot to 4 POSTs from an out-of-band layer (not the fork's schedule); terminate bounded+visible regardless. Recommend r2/r4 adjudication before install decision; consider a follow-up to pin maxRetries=0 in the fork's SDK options if strict wire-level <=3 is required.","created_at":"2026-08-08T04:52:28.277419606Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:MsapjYVWz84JLdmDwtLdRfCTiGIRxuAX0zVYQJYG9U8","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg8TQCXWB922mhHqpOY+eTVkSoagnoAAUHyi8tNs6etHwAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAqtJ06KfoO9J8mhIapHA9yvsWFrrFjB3n0LHbhHRn6jTczpYQggQ2DSv9SiOqdHeD8J2h9g0J9G/tCWkIISdWDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:MsapjYVWz84JLdmDwtLdRfCTiGIRxuAX0zVYQJYG9U8","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg8TQCXWB922mhHqpOY+eTVkSoagnoAAUHyi8tNs6etHwAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGes2Cz0YQ5OmS3XAgRNO+TgDYPYJ7XsbqvNmbL9YJD82rwhSx1gkEERpQnSwr2Ejw9ra5uh+mgW7tzexqJYsw8="}
